The Village of the Munchkins is reached by a one-use magic portal hidden 
inside an Air Elemental that shows up suspiciously early and is only 
available if Munchkins (h) have not been genoed yet.

The hero (and pet if adjacent) are swept away to the Village instead of 
being pummeled to death and the magical Air Elemental vanishes.

The Munchkins have the physical attributes of hobbits, but their 
behavior is quite different.  Each Munchkin is generated with a random 
cursed (1:0) wand.  The Munchkins are always generated hostile and will 
chase after the hero zapping their wands at the hero (regardless of the 
type of wand) over and over again until the wand explodes or the final 
charge is used.  If a Munchkin gets a wish they will wish for a Wand of 
Death, which will also be cursed(1:0).

If the Munchkins are unable to use a wand then they will still chase 
after the hero and use their second and even more insidious attack. 
Once within seven spaces of the hero they will quote a random rumor, but 
two thirds of the time this will be from the false rumor file.  Any hero 
who has her Wisdom abused below 3 on this level dies.  If canceled the 
Munchkins will use their final attack of hitting the hero with their 
tiny fists.

Having dealt with the Munchkins the hero will then face the boss of this 
level, the Wacky Witch of the West.  (Who has been driven a little daft 
by the Munchkins.)  She is a hostile 10th level wizard with robe, one 
random ring (50% of the time this will be whatever silver is), one 
random wand (fully charged, also silver half the time), a dagger (50% 
silver, otherwise random with a 5% chance of athane), a button labeled 
"#2" (attempting to apply this gives the message "You don't feel like 
being a number") and the silver slippers artifact.

The silver slippers do silver damage when kicking, grant Magic 
Resistance, and when invoked provide a realm teleport that only works 
between Oz (the Village being the first level of Oz) and the hero's 
quest and fails when invoked anyplace other than these two realms.  Each 
such realm teleport drops the hero off at a random spot in the first 
level of the destination realm.

